//RS // `DBValue` mirrors `JSON`'s dynamic-value construction mechanism
//RS // (`DBValue.Int(n)` / `.Float(f)` / `.Text(s)` / `.Bool(b)` / `.Blob(bytes)` /
//RS // `.Null`) but is SQL-shaped: `Int` keeps the full 64-bit width SQLite integers
//RS // carry (never routed through `f64`, which would lose precision above 2^53).
//RS // `Blob` carries an exact `[U8]` sequence. A `Row` is `Map<String, DBValue>` —
//RS // the built-in `Map` type already gives `.get`/`.keys`/`.values`, so no separate
//RS // nominal `Row` type is needed (I8). Keep the Rust carrier behind one adapter
//RS // alias so generated callers never depend on the backing map implementation.
